  "notes": "FORMS:\n{鎮痛|ちんつう} (pain relief) + {剤|ざい} (medicine, agent). The suffix ～{剤|ざい} is used for various types of medicines and chemical agents.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {鎮痛剤|ちんつうざい}を{飲|の}む (to take a painkiller)\n- {鎮痛剤|ちんつうざい}を{処方|しょほう}する (to prescribe painkillers)\n- {市販|しはん}の{鎮痛剤|ちんつうざい} (over-the-counter painkillers)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {痛|いた}み{止|ど}め (pain reliever — more casual synonym)\n- {解熱鎮痛剤|げねつちんつうざい} (fever and pain reducer)",
